Description: Implementation of the Future API <doi:10.32614/RJ-2021-048> on
    top of the 'batchtools' package. The backend is fully compliant with the
    Future API, as validated by the 'future.tests' conformance test suite,
    meaning that code using futures gives identical results and behaves the
    same regardless of which future backend is used. Futures are resolved on
    the local machine, on an ad-hoc cluster of machines, or via job
    schedulers on high-performance compute ('HPC') clusters, such as
    'Slurm', 'SGE', 'LSF', 'OpenLava', and 'TORQUE' / 'PBS'. A common use is
    to parallelize existing map-reduce calls via the 'futurize' package
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2601.17578>, e.g.
    'plan(future.batchtools::batchtools_slurm)' followed by 'lapply(xs, fcn)
    |> futurize()' or 'purrr::map(xs, fcn) |> futurize()'.
